q10.body:
Nobody has played AFTERFALL by hand yet. The scripted tour (`tools/run-unity-checks.sh tour`) drives commands directly, so it cannot tell us whether the game is fun, readable or well paced.

**What to do**
1. Download the macOS build from the [latest release](https://github.com/Ale-Newport/AfterFall/releases/latest), or open the project in Unity 6000.3.28f1 and press Play.
2. Play the acceptance scenario in [docs/TESTING.md](https://github.com/Ale-Newport/AfterFall/blob/main/docs/TESTING.md): bare hands → shelter → furnace → electricity → workshop → pump.
3. Comment here with:
   - time to the first construction and to the first machine output;
   - anything confusing (prompts, UI, what to do next);
   - movement, camera, harvest and colonist pacing, and the length of a day;
   - bugs, with steps (or open a bug report and link it).

Any amount of play helps; you do not need to finish the loop.

